==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage starts with Le'Solar, who should not be a real threat with enough [[Treasure]]s from CotC 1 and 2. Just be sure to have something that can break its Barrier. If you do that quickly enough, you can reach the enemy base in under a minute and just win from there. As this stage has no boss shockwave, you can quickly eliminate the base's 225,000 HP in no time once you reach it. Aside from Star Peng, none of the enemies here would be able to stop you since they would all burrow instead of attacking the Cats damaging the base, and even when they burrow, they would have no time to reach your base.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can work together to destroy Lophiiformes, though any [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayer Cats]] work as well. You also want a [[Barrier Breaker]] so you don't have to brute force your way through Le'Solar, preferably one with low~moderate range to they can get into Ribbo's blind spot. These combined with a generalized lineup of [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Anti-Zombie Cats]] should lead you to victory.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage can be cheesed with Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and Money Up [[Cat Combo]]s. Bring [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] to kill the starting Trolly Bloggers, then use [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]] or any other [[Barrier Breaker]] for the UltraBaaBaa. This will cause the Deathshund to burrow. You will need to spawn Awakened Bahamut Cat as fast as possible before the Deathshund burrows back up. This will cause Awakened Bahamut Cat to go past the Deathshund and repeatedly damage the base until you win. Make sure to keep meatshielding so that the Deathshund won't destroy your base.

